{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/20774-the-god-machine-s-anti-symbolism","id":20774,"title":"The God Machine's Anti-Symbolism","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-30T13:50:59-08:00","id":20774,"title":"The God Machine's Anti-Symbolism","content":"Bonjour,<br /> <br /> I may be running a game of Demon soon, which is exciting, but I wish to ensure I am fully understanding the aesthetics of the game. To that end, I would like to verify whether my reading of the God Machine is &quot;correct&quot; or at least cogent.<br /> <br /> So:<br /> <br /> The God Machine doesn't do symbolism. Form always follows function. In this way, it is nearly the antithesis of, say, Mage or Changeling, which rely heavily on symbolism (mystical in the former, narrative in the latter). If a piece of Infrastructure grows a tree that can cleanse the are it is planted in of pollution, it is not because trees are symbolic of nature's purifying power or what-have-you, but because encoded in the universe is some occult law of physics that causes the confluence of that tree placed in that location to cancel out the polluting phenomena. On the same note, though on the literary level that angels are made of machine parts might be symbolic of their conformist natures, the God Machine does not approach their construction with the same eye. A machine angel has those specific machine parts because they aid in its function. Mechanical hearts are more resilient and efficient than those made of meat, etc. The God Machine might not even understand the concept of exegetical symbolism. I imagine it is intelligent enough to recognize symbolism as an integral part of human psychology, and probably plans accordingly if a specific angel is needed for a specific task (i.e. capitalizing on the mythological infrastructure in place in India by giving a Messenger angel meant to amass a cult there the form of Kali or Shiva), but the idea of, say, dressing up a Psychopomp angel as a skeleton in Haitian funerary garb for its own aesthetic sake would probably never naturally occur to it.<br /> <br /> To summarize: Form follows function, and symbolism is (almost always) unnecessary window dressing in the God Machine's electronic eyes.<br /> <br /> Does this sound about right? If so, I wonder what sorts of implications the God Machine has for supernatural entities that do deal heavily in their own symbolism--Might Tale Crafting always fall apart when attempted on an angel, for instance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T14:51:19-08:00","id":20804,"title":"","content":"Well....Yes and no.<br /> <br /> THe thing of the matter is that while form follows function, the functions are inherently inherently somewhat strange and abstract to our eyes, and certainly a very large thing to the God Machine. Working off an (ill-remembered) example from Demon, just because you kill people at four clocktowers doesn't mean you automatically have the engine to fold space and time-the form has to line up in some way so that it has occult significance. We think of the Sephirot as a visual guide of Kabbalah's Ein Sof's manfiestations(putting it stupidly simple and somewhat incorrect), but to the God Machine it's just an extremely effective circuit board or something for reality.<br /> <br /> The point is that, yes, Form follows function, and occult symbolism is more a happy accident than a deliberate evocation, but that still doesn't mean the God Machine won't build Infrastructure in such a way that resembles a pentagram or something. After all, it works.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Or putting it another way, the work of the God Machine can be as symbolic or non-symbolic as you want, all justified by the higher knowledge of the Machine. I like to mix things up, use symbols as a base and then tweak it according to city/architechtural/computer board design- mixing the occult with the practical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-30-2013, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T16:20:33-08:00","id":20850,"title":"","content":"Within the GMC Framework, Occult symbolism is often just a trapping, except when it isn't, and it's actually a functionally necessary part of the equation.<br /> <br /> A God Machine project will be covered with mystic symbology, but only because those symbols are necessary parts of the energy channel, not because of any aesthetic.<br /> <br /> More to the point, within the framework of the GMC, all mystical symbols and trappings stem from the complex laws and backdoors of reality that the god machine uses. So if the God Machine uses the Tree-of-Life pattern we associate with Kabbalah magic, it's not that the God Machine is using Kabbalah to power it's infrastructure; It's that Kabbalah is using one of the God Machine's reality pathways to enact other magic. The God Machine doesn't make Angels in the image of gods, it made Angels in the form that was useful or necessary, and humans who survived or benefited from the projects they were sent to preform either built a religion around them or incorporated them into their existing religion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T18:28:11-08:00","id":20906,"title":"","content":"Short answer: yes. Long answer: An occult matrix may incorporate symbols that humans attribute meaning to. But the reason for said symbols is not because of what they represent, but because they are a necessary part of the Sufficiently Advanced science involved in the occult matrix. If anything, human symbolism may have developed from observation of these occult matrices. So the reason we associate trees with purification and life is because they are used in purifying occult matrices, and through observation and cultural osmosis we've become peripherally aware that trees have something to do with with cleansing. But the real reason the God Machine uses them that way in the first place is that there's some actual physical law it's exploiting. We just don't understand the science behind it, but in theory anyone who knew how it worked (and controlled implement the proper infrastructure) could achieve the se outcome by the same methods. Because it's all just science we don't yet comprehend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T19:02:54-08:00","id":21399,"title":"","content":"In other words, you're correct, however, because occult symbolism is often a functional part of supernatural physics, that sort of thing tends to crop up in God Machine Infrastructure, the same way that triangular shapes tend to show up in modern bridges.<br /> <br /> Also because it gives your Occult Investigator PCs something to go on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T08:49:24-08:00","id":21662,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your responses. I had neglected the Kaballah angle, which I think does dovetail nicely into G-M themes. I'm imagining the characters breaking open a computer in an Infrastructure library and finding the board circuits to be arranged into the Sephiroth. <br /> <br /> Speaking of symbolism in the game, it's hard to miss that the number four is most recurrent: Four Incarnations, four Agendas, four Cipher keys, etc. It's mentioned in the section on Ciphers that not a small number of demons consider the number to have special significance, and the God Machine is also aware of this. I wonder whence the number comes? It's recurring in Christianity/Judaism/Islam (four beasts, four matriarchs, Eid al-Adah lasts for four days, the Tetragrammaton), not to mention the number's importance in other cultures (the Four Noble Truths of Buddhism, four in Japanese is considered unlucky because it's a homophone for death), though all of those could be the result of G-M meddling to give demons something to drive themselves crazy with. On the other hand, four might actually have some occult significance that the G-M merely exploits. I guess for now it's up to the Storyteller to decide. The truth of the matter could definitely make for a decent Inquisitor's Cipher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T15:09:08-08:00","id":21917,"title":"","content":"In Hebrew symbology, four is the number that represents the earth.<br /> <br /> Make of that what you will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T15:35:33-08:00","id":21927,"title":"","content":"Well there's the &quot;Shma&quot; prayer that refers to the angels and goes (roughly translated from hebrew): Michael to my right, Gabriel to my left, Uriel to my front, Raphael to my back, above me - God's spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1348-hecktar","name":"Hecktar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T15:43:13-08:00","id":21934,"title":"","content":"according to what I learned in high school, 4 is a strong typological number in Judaism. It is, in many ways, present the maximal limit of thing- like a prophesy about three vile acts God has forgiven, but the fourth is too much. Other examples are the Flood (which happened for 40 nights) and the Exodus (traveling in the desert for 40 years). According to some biblical researchers, 4 (and the numbers which contain it) present the limit, the boundary of understanding before things become so much that one can't divide them, It like the eternal asking of &quot;when does a group of things turns from &quot;few&quot; into &quot;many&quot;- and the answer is 4.<br /> <br /> And if I'm mistaken, I blame my bible teacher :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T15:50:38-08:00","id":21940,"title":"","content":"The Seers of the Throne like their hierarchies to run in fours as well...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To summarize: Form follows function, and symbolism is (almost always) unnecessary window dressing in the God Machine's electronic eyes. </div> </div> </div>Maybe, maybe not. If Changeling or Mage cosmology is correct then symbolism has actual utility, it's a part of how reality works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T08:44:18-08:00","id":22364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/20774-the-god-machine-s-anti-symbolism?p=21940#post21940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe, maybe not. If Changeling or Mage cosmology is correct then symbolism has actual utility, it's a part of how reality works.</div> </div> </div> </div>The symbolism between all three lines is wildly diverse, however. In Changeling, symbolism is usually derived from an object/phenomenon's perceived qualities. Stone is associated with strength, spring with renewal. In Mage, the symbolism is a bit more...abstracted? I'm not as familiar with Mage, and I have yet to read Imperial Mysteries, which seems to contain most of the overarching information on the Supernal setting, so I'm not entirely clear on how it works, though willworking seems to work better if you have the right correspondences, though their appearance in the phenomenal world seems to be almost incidental to their true forms in the higher realms. Or something. To quote a drunk teenage girl: &quot;The symbols hol dall the power.&quot;<br /> <br /> All three game lines seem to hold a different set of truths as <i>prima facie</i>. Which is fine, since all three have different themes. I'm just trying to work them out conceptually. For Demon (or the God Machine, at least) everything is physics. Really weird physics, but physics all the same. Changeling is more concerned with aesthetics; the Wyrd wants interesting stories, not mathematical proofs. Mage is after the deeper, philosophical truths, which connect together all aesthetics and make quantifiable science incidental/trivial. <br /> <br /> It becomes a chicken/egg question with regards to symbols and reality, and each line has a different answer to it. I guess that level of metaphysics only matters for crossover games though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T11:21:47-08:00","id":22453,"title":"","content":"Interesting that you bring in Mage and Changeling, while discussing the symbologies present, and how 4 is a sacred number to the Machine. while 5 seems to be the primary number of power in most games, 4 makes its presence known in both of those games, especially as a number of &quot;order&quot;, or other things associated with the Machine (safety, &quot;rightness&quot;; control). in Mage, four is the number important to the seers, their ministries, and tetrarchies--which makes sense, as the Seers are often on the same side as the Machine (if they, and the exarchs, aren't directly servants and gears, which they might be). similarly, the atlantean diamond could be seen as more old fashioned, precise, controlled, and orderly (and, in some eyes, more proper) than the pentacle. stronger and more stable. In changeling, there are quite a handful of seemings, but the Courts that bring order to the cities, keep reality from breaking down and allowing fae invasion, and generally protect and control changelings--again, we come to four in most court systems. four directions, four elements, four seasons, four times of day, four suits of cards..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T16:00:56-08:00","id":22677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/20774-the-god-machine-s-anti-symbolism?p=22453#post22453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In changeling, there are quite a handful of seemings, but the Courts that bring order to the cities, keep reality from breaking down and allowing fae invasion, and generally protect and control changelings--again, we come to four in most court systems. four directions, four elements, four seasons, four times of day, four suits of cards..</div> </div> </div> </div>Which could explain why the Solstice-wannabe-Court is made out of anarchists and similar types, if I remember correctly","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T18:51:29-08:00","id":22804,"title":"","content":"The way I think of it is in terms of the source of their powers. The god machine, as people have mentioned before, only uses symbolism where it's relevant to the occult matrix being created, and some mortals have stumbled onto the power these symbols hold and called them magic or art (I like to think that thaumaturges from second sight have just managed to figure out how to work some very basic, reliable occult matracies). The important thing about the god machine's power is that it's not external like it is for mages and changelings, it's using forces present in our universe that are simply beyond our understanding. mages call down higher truths from the supernal realms, where concepts flow more freely, so they get more utility from symbolism. The wyrd uses narratives kind of like the god machine uses infrastructure sometimes, which is where talecrafting and the like comes from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/807-arcadianawakened","name":"ArcadianAwakened","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T06:04:33-08:00","id":23093,"title":"","content":"The Supernal isn't external to our universe, it IS our universe. It's like saying maths is external to the universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T06:48:36-08:00","id":23112,"title":"","content":"To an extent math is external to our universe. If every physical thing in the universe were destroyed tomorrow, <i>a priori</i> mathematical principles would still persist, even with no one or nothing around to carry them out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T07:29:55-08:00","id":23136,"title":"","content":"I don't think that first point follows from the second. Whether it transcends it or not, mathematical principles are still a fundamental element making up the universe.<br /> <br /> At least for the Mage cosmology, the supernal isn't another world which creeps into the material world, in a sense it IS the material world. A world without the supernal would be like a universe that doesn't have any patterns to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T08:11:53-08:00","id":23155,"title":"","content":"I view the Supernal more as a realm of Platonic Ideals, much like how Fae Arcadia is a realm of pure Story. It may be <i>connected to</i> the Fallen World, but it isn't actually a <i>part of</i> the Fallen World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T08:30:52-08:00","id":23167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/20774-the-god-machine-s-anti-symbolism?p=23136#post23136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that first point follows from the second. Whether it transcends it or not, mathematical principles are still a fundamental element making up the universe.<br /> <br /> At least for the Mage cosmology, the supernal isn't another world which creeps into the material world, in a sense it IS the material world. A world without the supernal would be like a universe that doesn't have any patterns to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I see. Like I mentioned before, I haven't read <i>Imperial Mysteries</i> so a lot of the higher-up Mage stuff still escapes me. I might still be missing the point of what you are saying here, but if the physical universe were destroyed, would the Supernal Realms still persist, or would they wink out of existence because every instance of their symbols is gone?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Just to clarify what I meant by the math thing, 2 + 2 = 4 would still be true even if there were no representations of 2, or 4, or addition. So, in Stygia, there is the symbol for &quot;ghost&quot;. If every ghost were to cease existing, would that symbol still be cogent or would it also cease to exist by dint of the non-existence of every ghost? My first impression is that the answer differs whether we're talking about every <i>current</i> ghost or every <i>possible</i> ghost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":". 12-04-2013, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T09:10:08-08:00","id":23182,"title":"","content":"This is a significant point of debate in Mage. The Supernal definitely used to be part of the world, but not so much any more, because Atlantis. Is that just a wound to be closed, or a clean cut to be crossed?) Hard to say. It lies 'truthward' of the material world (the Lower Depths are in the other direction, which probably has something to do with why inferno demons gain definition -after- being summoned). I'm not sure you can really say which one is dependent on the other - there's arguments for several models. I'd guess, though, that the more plausible scenarios for the removal of the Supernal Realms end with a new version springing forth from the Lower Depths or the Abyss. There's not a shortage of things that want to define the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T10:43:29-08:00","id":23224,"title":"","content":"I don't think &quot;part of the world&quot; or &quot;not part of the world&quot; are really applicable concepts to the supernal realms, given that they are not actually places. They are collections of symbols that make up the concepts and laws that govern our world. It's no more part or not part of our world than the internet is part or not part of your computer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T21:54:17-08:00","id":23528,"title":"","content":"I could probably map the different possible implications of the Supernal Realm's reflections on the Fallen World in terms of the different assumptions that generate the different systems of metaphysical symbolic logic, but I don't like the Mage cosmology so I leave that to someone more interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}